## Architectural correction before any #958 outcome

The long diagnostic was stopped incomplete after approximately 5h16m and is recorded as `NOT_RUN`: it emitted no terminal report or checkpoint, and no fit began. Its outcomes no longer had decision value once the deployed path was shown to be the wrong abstraction.

A deep audit of the original Prime Router and its retained design material establishes the intended mechanism:

- the ordered Riemann zeta zeros are the immutable spectral grid;
- semantic atoms map to primes; semiprimes are transition experts and higher prime n-lets carry the combinatorial/Hamiltonian context;
- the deployed geometry is the R4 approximation, while UOR/E8 is the broader target; this does not assert that the implementation is literally H4 x H4;
- data is bound to its geometric location as compiled harmonic/spin state;
- only torsion/spin evolves: a node applies the local quaternionic/Lie-group delta rather than recomputing the absolute geometry of the whole history;
- decoding is causal route continuation: previous route -> next route, previous two routes -> next route, and sentence route/holonomy -> next route;
- candidate work is restricted to the current divisor/n-let neighborhood and selected by least local energy.

The legacy live code contains pieces of this idea (fixed zeta basis, prime products, first/second-order transitions, evolving R4/Hopf telemetry), but it scans stored corpus items for retrieval, stores text plus 512-vectors in a cache, and uses word trigrams for geometric-only output. Hopf/spin state is not the load-bearing storage address. The current layer-29 mixer is farther away: learned dense query/key projections create four-vector coordinates and then score prior positions.

Therefore #958 will not fit another learned Q/K representation. The redesign must first prove, source-free:

1. a versioned, content-addressed compiled-spin manifest binds the fixed zeta grid, prime/n-let expert, payload, harmonic coefficients, R4 spin/torsion state, kappa/witness, and provenance;
2. changing torsion changes the selected local route but cannot change the grid identity or payload identity;
3. direct last-one, last-two, and sentence-route lookup is deterministic, causal, and bounded, with no all-corpus/all-prefix scan;
4. semiprime divisors and ordered n-let overlap define every allowed continuation, with direction retained by spin/ordered-path state;
5. matched context permutation and torsion-null controls change the continuation where predeclared;
6. compile is deterministic across one and four workers, then a release-only four-worker canary reports throughput, progress, ETA, checkpoint/resume, and a hard cost ceiling;
7. a bounded chat probe demonstrates whether this route-state decoder itself produces prompt-responsive text. Fluency from Ollama or the remaining source transformer cannot count as a pass.

This abandons the current learned layerwise-replacement representation, not geometric decoding. No expensive source run is authorized until these gates exist and pass.
